{"tool_name":"onestoprnaseq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"onestoprnaseq","home":"https://mccb.umassmed.edu/OneStopRNAseq","summary":"A Web Application for Comprehensive and Efficient Analyses of RNA-Seq Data.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T11:24:32Z","last_update_date":"2021-03-13T19:13:30Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access (with restrictions)","biotools_curie":"biotools:onestoprnaseq","credit":[{"email":"julie.zhu@umassmed.edu","name":"Lihua Julie Zhu","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7416-0590","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Alternative splicing prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0264"},{"term":"Differential gene expression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3223"},{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"},{"term":"RNA-Seq analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3680"},{"term":"RNA-Seq quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3800"}]}],"name":"OneStopRNAseq","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.3390/GENES11101165","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 by the authors. Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland.Over the past decade, a large amount of RNA sequencing (RNA\u2010seq) data were deposited in public repositories, and more are being produced at an unprecedented rate. However, there are few open source tools with point\u2010and\u2010click interfaces that are versatile and offer streamlined comprehensive analysis of RNA\u2010seq datasets. To maximize the capitalization of these vast public resources and facilitate the analysis of RNA\u2010seq data by biologists, we developed a web application called OneStopRNAseq for the one\u2010stop analysis of RNA\u2010seq data. OneStopRNAseq has user\u2010friendly interfaces and offers workflows for common types of RNA\u2010seq data analyses, such as comprehensive data\u2010quality control, differential analysis of gene expression, exon usage, alternative splicing, transposable element expression, allele\u2010specific gene expression quantification, and gene set enrichment analysis. Users only need to select the desired analyses and genome build, and provide a Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO) accession number or Dropbox links to sequence files, alignment files, gene\u2010expression\u2010count tables, or rank files with the corresponding metadata. Our pipeline facilitates the comprehensive and efficient analysis of private and public RNA\u2010seq data.","authors":[{"name":"Green M.R."},{"name":"Hu K."},{"name":"Li R."},{"name":"Liu H."},{"name":"Zhu L.J."}],"citationCount":3,"date":"2020-10-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genes","title":"Onestoprnaseq: A web application for comprehensive and efficient analyses of rna\u2010seq data"},"pmcid":"PMC7650687","pmid":"33023248"}],"topic":[{"term":"Functional, regulatory and non-coding RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0659"},{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"OneStopRNAseq","home":"https://bio.tools/onestoprnaseq","summary":"A Web Application for Comprehensive and Efficient Analyses of RNA-Seq Data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:onestoprnaseq/cmd/mccb.umassmed.edu","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":31,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":3,"year":"2026"},{"count":4,"year":"2022"},{"count":5,"year":"2021"},{"c